# Midscene model config — LOCAL. No API key, no per-run cost, nothing to rotate.
#
# The key below is a placeholder: Ollama's OpenAI-compatible endpoint requires
# the header to exist and ignores its value. That is the point of running the
# vision model locally — QA can run unattended without a real credential ever
# being involved, so there is nothing to leak and nothing to rotate.
MIDSCENE_MODEL_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
MIDSCENE_MODEL_NAME=qwen2.5vl:7b
MIDSCENE_MODEL_FAMILY=qwen2.5-vl
MIDSCENE_MODEL_API_KEY=ollama-local-no-key-needed
MIDSCENE_MODEL_TIMEOUT=180000
MIDSCENE_MODEL_RETRY_COUNT=2

# ── The measured alternative, deliberately NOT the default. [H-016 · 2026-08-19]
#
# `qwen2.5vl:7b` above was chosen because it needs no key, which is an
# availability choice, not a measured one. delta measured it: it catches
# **53%** of planted screen defects and hits **45%** of click targets, landing
# on the wrong control 16% of the time. Roughly half of every planted defect
# goes unreported, and a missed defect is silent where a false alarm is loud.
#
# Routing each step to the model measured best AT THAT STEP does better:
#
#   MIDSCENE_MODEL_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787/v1
#   MIDSCENE_MODEL_NAME=delta/auto
#   # and first:  cd 02-Projects/delta/code && python3 -m delta.serve
#
# Measured 2026-08-19 by `python3 -m delta.route_table`, all three numbers:
#   judging  → google/gemma-3-12b-it  catch 83%, FALSE ALARM 21%, $0.00228/run
#   pointing → amazon/nova-lite-v1    hit 62%, wrong control 19%, $0.01074/run
#   (reference anthropic/claude-sonnet-5: catch 91% / false alarm 9%, $0.34/run)
#
# **Why it is not switched on: this lane is free today and that lane is not.**
# It routes over OpenRouter on the owner's key, so it turns a $0 unattended run into
# a paid one — a few tenths of a cent per run, but zero to non-zero is his call,
# not an agent's. The 21% false-alarm rate is also four times the loud half of
# the tradeoff; it is survivable only because the protocol already requires a
# failed vision assertion to reproduce deterministically before anything is
# fixed. Switch it on by editing the two lines above, not by editing this note.
